1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,134
This is a boarding party.

2
00:00:03,034 --> 00:00:05,149
The ship is alongside a dead hulk,

3
00:00:05,599 --> 00:00:09,375
and the Engineering console has just gone aboard as Chief Okoro.

4
00:00:11,175 --> 00:00:14,532
He's the person who sits at Engineering in this story,

5
00:00:14,982 --> 00:00:16,953
on the bridge and on the hulk.

6
00:00:18,753 --> 00:00:21,625
Last time you played a scene somebody else wrote.

7
00:00:22,525 --> 00:00:25,810
Today you write your own: who goes, where they go,

8
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:28,141
and the few lines that start it.

9
00:00:29,341 --> 00:00:30,765
First, who goes.

10
00:00:31,665 --> 00:00:34,664
This is the Engineering console at the start of the game,

11
00:00:35,114 --> 00:00:39,367
and the name at the top, Chief Okoro, is a name I wrote.

12
00:00:41,167 --> 00:00:44,249
I go to the end of my fact sheet and add a section,

13
00:00:44,699 --> 00:00:48,869
and the first line inside its fence is one bare word, crew.

14
00:00:49,769 --> 00:00:51,483
Then the ship these people crew,

15
00:00:51,933 --> 00:00:54,614
and a line that says the names are locked.

16
00:00:56,414 --> 00:00:58,494
Under it, one record for each person.

17
00:00:59,394 --> 00:01:01,740
Each one says which console they sit at,

18
00:01:02,190 --> 00:01:04,233
what they look like, and their job.

19
00:01:05,133 --> 00:01:09,371
So whoever sits at Engineering tonight is Chief Okoro,

20
00:01:09,821 --> 00:01:11,794
on the bridge and aboard the hulk.

21
00:01:12,694 --> 00:01:14,721
There's one cast, and it's the crew.

22
00:01:15,921 --> 00:01:17,103
Now, where they go.

23
00:01:18,003 --> 00:01:21,442
On the handheld, the bar names the room, The Airlock,

24
00:01:21,892 --> 00:01:24,994
and under it there's one line and three buttons.

25
00:01:25,894 --> 00:01:27,845
All of that is one record I write.

26
00:01:29,645 --> 00:01:31,700
A place is a section of rooms,

27
00:01:32,150 --> 00:01:34,890
and a room is the simplest record you've written yet.

28
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:36,688
It has no fence at all.

29
00:01:38,488 --> 00:01:42,241
One line that starts with a percent sign is what the party finds.

30
00:01:43,141 --> 00:01:46,530
Each line that starts with a dash is a way out:

31
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:49,601
the words in square brackets go on a button,

32
00:01:50,051 --> 00:01:53,821
and the key in round brackets names the room it leads to.

33
00:01:55,621 --> 00:01:58,487
And this one has nothing in its round brackets.

34
00:01:58,937 --> 00:02:02,577
On the handheld, it's the Return to the ship button.

35
00:02:03,477 --> 00:02:06,567
It leads nowhere, and taking it ends the visit.

36
00:02:07,767 --> 00:02:09,812
I save, and I run lint,

37
00:02:10,262 --> 00:02:12,423
and for once it isn't clean.

38
00:02:13,323 --> 00:02:16,925
It says nothing in this mission reads a section with this key,

39
00:02:17,375 --> 00:02:20,547
so my rooms are never loaded. That's true.

40
00:02:21,447 --> 00:02:23,289
Nothing does read them yet.

41
00:02:23,739 --> 00:02:25,808
So I leave the key exactly as it is,

42
00:02:26,258 --> 00:02:28,754
and I go and add the thing that reads it.

43
00:02:29,954 --> 00:02:31,724
Before that, two rules.

44
00:02:32,624 --> 00:02:34,772
One: every room has a way back.

45
00:02:35,672 --> 00:02:38,938
In the reactor room, the handheld has one button,

46
00:02:39,388 --> 00:02:41,694
and it's the way back to the airlock.

47
00:02:42,594 --> 00:02:45,245
A room with no way out holds the party for good,

48
00:02:45,695 --> 00:02:47,121
and lint won't tell you.

49
00:02:48,921 --> 00:02:52,478
Two: the way home goes where leaving is a decision.

50
00:02:53,378 --> 00:02:56,018
One press of that button, by anyone,

51
00:02:56,468 --> 00:03:00,118
ends the visit for everybody, and the place isn't offered again.

52
00:03:01,018 --> 00:03:03,901
So it's in the room they arrive in,

53
00:03:04,351 --> 00:03:05,674
and nowhere else for now.

54
00:03:06,874 --> 00:03:07,657
Now the start.

55
00:03:08,557 --> 00:03:13,743
On Helm, the handheld's Quest Log has a step called Close Inspection,

56
00:03:14,193 --> 00:03:17,066
with a picture of the hulk and two short paragraphs.

57
00:03:18,866 --> 00:03:21,441
It's a quest of the kind you wrote in Class 1:

58
00:03:21,891 --> 00:03:24,240
bring the ship within five hundred of the hulk.

59
00:03:25,140 --> 00:03:26,596
The new line is this one.

60
00:03:27,046 --> 00:03:29,557
When the quest completes, it sends a signal,

61
00:03:30,007 --> 00:03:31,818
and I've named it board hulk.

62
00:03:33,618 --> 00:03:36,476
The description's a page, the way it was in Class 1.

63
00:03:37,376 --> 00:03:39,793
A picture of the hulk at the top,

64
00:03:40,243 --> 00:03:42,171
then two short paragraphs.

65
00:03:43,071 --> 00:03:46,614
The second one tells the crew a party can cross,

66
00:03:47,064 --> 00:03:48,960
so they think about who goes.

67
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:56,094
When the quest completes, Engineering's handheld has a tile called Boarding Party,

68
00:03:56,545 --> 00:03:58,950
offering a visit called The Hulk.

69
00:03:59,850 --> 00:04:01,862
One recipe card makes that happen.

70
00:04:02,312 --> 00:04:05,432
I open the story file, go to the very end, and paste it.

71
00:04:06,332 --> 00:04:07,235
I don't read it.

72
00:04:07,685 --> 00:04:11,772
I change three things on it, and they're on the page: the signal's name,

73
00:04:12,222 --> 00:04:14,738
the key of the room the party arrives in,

74
00:04:15,188 --> 00:04:16,970
and the name the crew sees on the tile.

75
00:04:18,770 --> 00:04:20,997
I run lint again, and now it's clean.

76
00:04:22,197 --> 00:04:26,319
I start the game with a server, a Helm and an Engineering console.

77
00:04:27,219 --> 00:04:29,973
And there's my name, before I've flown anywhere.

78
00:04:31,773 --> 00:04:33,230
I bring the ship in close,

79
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:35,236
and the quest completes.

80
00:04:36,136 --> 00:04:38,685
On Engineering I open the handheld,

81
00:04:39,135 --> 00:04:44,196
and there's a Boarding Party tile offering The Hulk. I beam down.

82
00:04:45,996 --> 00:04:48,420
Now this console is the party's handheld.

83
00:04:48,870 --> 00:04:52,446
It says who I am, my job, and the room I'm in,

84
00:04:52,896 --> 00:04:56,149
and under that is my line, with a button for each way out.

85
00:04:57,049 --> 00:05:00,663
I go aft, and the page keeps what I've read.

86
00:05:01,563 --> 00:05:04,126
Back, forward, back again.

87
00:05:05,926 --> 00:05:07,858
And from the airlock, I go home,

88
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:10,327
and the console is back at Engineering.

89
00:05:11,527 --> 00:05:15,276
Your turn. Add a fourth room, with a way in and a way back,

90
00:05:15,726 --> 00:05:20,325
and add a third person to your roster, at Helm, with a job you make up.

91
00:05:22,125 --> 00:05:25,012
Then break it on purpose.

92
00:05:25,462 --> 00:05:27,515
Delete the way back from your new room,

93
00:05:27,965 --> 00:05:30,760
run lint, and read the word clean.

94
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:34,671
Then walk into that room, and see what your crew would see.

95
00:05:36,471 --> 00:05:38,888
Next time, everyone gets a different menu.
